<article class="env-proposition" id="096916">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/096916">Proposition <span data-tag="096916">5.5.3.10</span>.</a>presentable!overcategoriesovercategory!of presentable $\infty $-categories Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category, and let $p: K \rightarrow \calC $ be a diagram in $\calC $ indexed by a (small) simplicial set $K$. If $\calC $ is presentable, then the $\infty $-category $\calC _{/p}$ is also presentable. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Corollary <a href="/tag/822A8A" data-tag="822A8A">5.4.6.7</a>, $\calC _{/p}$ is accessible. The existence of small colimits in $\calC _{/p}$ follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/9233A3" data-tag="9233A3">1.2.13.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>